{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789546160,"nonce":"XflanlFlWXVuVxki/L3QMHs/ThA=","title":"A module global E used in a function default crashes zypy","message":"The unedited meteor-contest kernel now gets past bisect and frozenset lowering but exits with signal 10 (status 138) before printing a timing. Reducing the source shows the signal starts with the rotate function default `rd={E: NE, ...}`; it occurs before any call. Minimal reproducer:\n\n    E = 2\n    def f(d=E):\n        return d\n    print(\"ok\")\n\nOn zypy this exits with signal 10. CPython prints ok. Replacing E with A, B, C, D, F, G, H, X, Y, Z, or T does not signal. A module-level read or dictionary using E works, so the interaction is specifically with a default expression. A default `d={E: 3}` also signals. This blocks a checked meteor-contest speed verdict. Investigate the type registry/compiler use of E as a generic parameter; that is a hypothesis, not yet a proven cause. Related frozenset issue a6c87be and speed-center index 89aaf85.","files":null}]}